      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:ef8cb6d97ad0db0b",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say \"we speak.\" (Hablamos.) And \"I eat.\" (Como.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: the same -mos, a different vowel",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Drop the -er, add -emos:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "comemos — we eat."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The -mos is the one you already have from hablamos. Only the vowel in front of it changed, from a to e — and it changed for the reason it always does: the ending takes the colour of its family."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That is the pattern for every plural ending you will meet. -mos and -n never change. The vowel before them does."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Something is about to happen that has not happened before. In the singular, -er and -ir were identical — como/comes/come and vivo/vives/vive, the same three endings twice over. That was a genuine saving, and it is about to stop. The next lesson is where the two families finally part."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "\"hablamos\" then \"comemos\" — the same -mos, a different vowel",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: \"hablamos\" then \"comemos\" — the same *-mos*, a different vowel]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C07-comemos-form",
              "prompt": "Turn comer into we eat.",
              "assesses": [
