              "feedback": {
                "correct": "Yes — only the vowel before it changes.",
                "incorrect": "The -mos. Only the vowel in front of it moves."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What is \"we eat\"? (Comemos.) Which part of a plural ending never changes? (The -mos.) And what has been true of -er and -ir until now? (They were identical — which the next lesson ends.)"
            }
          ]
        }
